<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore bunkers steady amid dull trade.</title>
<headline>Singapore bunkers steady amid dull trade.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore bunker quotes on Friday were steady amid dull demand, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;Enquiries are poor and trade is slow,&quot; said on oil major.</p>
<p>Bunker 380-cst was quoted at $97.50 by a European major and at $96 per tonne by a U.S major.</p>
<p>Bunker 180-cst were quoted at betwen $102-$104.50, around Thursday's levels.</p>
<p>MDO and gas oil were quoted lower to $170/$175 and $180/$183 per tonne respectively.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (65-870 3082)</p>
